close_reason: "Fixed in PR #1779: recovery commands follow a declared shell dialect with a cmd.exe-safe caret form, unjudgeable holder activity reports state unknown, and a release by the holder a close ended keeps the later holder's claim"
contract_change:
  api: "pm release, pm claim refusals (claim_activity) and rendered recovery commands on Windows"
  before: "A release by the holder a close ended cleared a later holder (warn policy, or strict with --force) and a --handoff or --pause from it moved the later holder work; claim_activity had no activity state and text refusals called an unjudgeable holder active; cmd.exe recovery commands left %VAR% and inner quotes live"
  after: "While the item history proves that a close ended the caller claim, that release writes nothing and warns release_claim_ended_by_close:<id>:<holder>, and a --handoff or --pause from it is refused with release_claim_ended_by_close before any write; after history-compact folds the claim and the close into a baseline, or when the history cannot be replayed, the ownership policy applies as for any other non-holder release. claim_activity.state (optional for older producers) is active, stale or unknown, and text refusals print activity unknown with its cause; an argument holding % or a double quote renders in the cmd.exe caret form"
  migrate: "Read claim_activity.state instead of inferring activity from stale_policy.stale; treat the release_claim_ended_by_close warning as a successful no-op and the refusal as the later holder owning the item; to take a later holder claim, use pm claim <id> --force and then release"
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_added
  owner: pm-gh1774
  gate_id: rendered-command-shell-safety
  negative_control: "tests/integration/cli/rendered-command-shell-safety.integration.spec.ts runs a hostile corpus with a defined probe variable through cmd.exe /d /s /c on the Windows native cohort and asserts byte-exact argv; on 2026.11.24 the %VAR% tracker path expands. tests/unit/commands/lifecycle/claim-command.spec.ts pins the close, force-claim, release sequence under default and strict policy with and without --force, asserting byte-identical item and history files, with negative controls for takeover-ended claims, strangers and unreadable streams. tests/unit/commands/lifecycle/claim-stale-takeover.spec.ts pins state unknown and the activity unknown text for an unreadable stream"
  local_checks[1]: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/cli/argv-utils.spec.ts tests/unit/commands/lifecycle/claim-command.spec.ts tests/unit/commands/lifecycle/claim-stale-takeover.spec.ts tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/claim-ownership-activity.spec.ts tests/integration/cli/rendered-command-shell-safety.integration.spec.ts
  hosted_checks[2]: "Windows regression cohort (native 1/1, Node 24)",Gates (coverage)
